Now I can see the full structure. The `$root: &` is `.no-sub-works`. The gallery item is `.no-sub-works__gallery-item` and the img figure is `.no-sub-works__gallery-item__img`.

The approach: add a CSS rule that forces `video { opacity: 0; transition: none }` when the parent `li` (`.no-sub-works__gallery-item`) is NOT being hovered.

In SCSS within `.no-sub-works__gallery-item`:

```scss
&:not(:hover) &__img video {
  // this would be: .no-sub-works__gallery-item:not(:hover) .no-sub-works__gallery-item__img video


```

Actually, it's easier to just write it within `&__img`:

```scss
&__img {
  // existing styles...

  &.is-video-active video {
    opacity: 1;
    transition: opacity 0.35s ease;
  }
